Bundled model and tokenizer
The bundled model is a modified and quantized descendant of
nkthebass/tinybrainbot-10m-v2-base, published by nkthebass with an
Apache-2.0 declaration in its model card:
https://huggingface.co/nkthebass/tinybrainbot-10m-v2-base
Audited model-card revision: 617e0f06dfe57f3c519be75177bfd8ca8a715530.
Upstream ownership and applicable notices are retained; no affiliation or
endorsement is implied. No separate upstream LICENSE or NOTICE file was
present in the audited base-model repository.

Modification notice: the upstream weights were continued on WikiText,
chat/arithmetic data and locally constructed examples, then fine-tuned
through the combined, Python, brainrot, brainrot-full and brainrot-v2
stages. The final checkpoint was converted to signed int8 rows with
float32 scales for this independent Java runtime. The tokenizer's
representation was also converted. These are not the original base weights.
See MODEL_LICENSE.md and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for scope, provenance,
known upstream terms and unresolved training-data permissions.

Dataset acknowledgements
TinyBrainBot's published pretraining sources include DCLM-Ultra,
DCLM-Ultra-1.1, FineWeb-Edu, Cosmopedia, TinyStories, Wikipedia,
Orca-Math and UltraData-Math, plus author-described distilled/synthetic sets.
Local fine-tuning used WikiText (Stephen Merity, Caiming Xiong,
James Bradbury and Richard Socher; Wikipedia contributors),
smol-smoltalk (HuggingFaceTB and its upstream contributors), and
basic-arithmetic (Chris McCormick).

The model's published provenance includes information from FineWeb-Edu
https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-edu
and DCLM-pro https://huggingface.co/datasets/gair-prox/DCLM-pro,
which declare the ODC Attribution License:
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/ .
Current smol-smoltalk also includes self-oss-instruct data originating from
https://huggingface.co/datasets/bigcode/self-oss-instruct-sc2-exec-filter-50k,
which declares that license. These are precautionary provenance/attribution
notices, not a claim that particular historical training rows are verified.

